            <div xml:id="d398">

                <pb facs="0475" n="357" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg357"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00Sonora/187: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Ciudad Juarez</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Dye</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">El
                                Paso, Tex</hi></placeName>., <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-03-10T16:00:00-07:00">March 10, 1929—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:43 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Have verified deaths Lydia Rodarte, American, two years old, in El Paso and
                    Theodore Barnes, American adult non-combatant in Juarez, due directly bullets in
                    battle of 8th instant, also serious wounding [of] Luis Chavez, American, six
                    years old, El Paso. Thirty-seven Federal officers, including three generals, two
                    hundred sixty-seven men and sixty-three women and children disarmed and given
                    asylum by General Moseley at Fort Bliss, are being splendidly cared for and are
                    contented and grateful.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dye</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
